      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "to “king Bhartṛihari, the protector of many people.” Bhartṛi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "hari gave it to his wife, she to her paramour; and he in his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "turn to a sweetheart of his, in whose hands Bhartṛihari saw the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "fruit. That was the occurrence which inspired this Stanza. The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "other commentator Râmarshi makes no mention of Vikrama in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "this connexion, but represents a Brahmin as giving the fruit to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Bhartṛihari, he to his wife, and so forth. मयि विरक्ता is noticeable ;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "it is equivalent to मद्विषयकविरागवती being an instance of the वैषयि-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "कसप्तमी (Siddh. Kaum. Târân. Ed. I. 307). अस्मत्कृते परितुष्यति is not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "quite clear. The commentator says मदर्थेपि काचन स्त्री मया सह सङ्गो",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "भवितव्य इति मनसि संतुष्टिं मानयिष्यति. Râmarshi (V. S. 105) says अस्म-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "त्कृतेपि अस्मदर्थेपि परितुष्यति समानन्दति अस्मास्वेव अनुरक्ता अस्मानेव अभिलषतीत्यर्थः.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "But these explanations are hardly satisfactory. As it stands, it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "perhaps may be taken to mean “is delighted with all I do.” But",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "the reading of X. is very much better. The hiatus at च इमाम् is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "worthy of note. Grammatically not incorrect, (see Siddh. Kaum.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "II. 22) it is disapproved of by writers on Rhetoric. See Kâvyâ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "dars'a (Bibl. Ind. Ed.) p. 430 and Kâvya Prakâs'a 155.—Va-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "santatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. III.—The commentator explains दुर्विदग्ध by गर्वित arrogant.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Rightly ; compare Kâdambarî p. 157. (Târânâth’s Ed.) ; also Pra-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "sannarâghava Nâṭaka p. 16 (Calc. Ed. 1872) where Râvaṇa calls",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the Bard who says he does not know him कतिपयग्रामटिकापर्यटनदुर्विदग्ध.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "Râmarshi explains it by दुश्चतुरः अर्धज्वलित इत्यर्थः which is also admis-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "sible,—‘imperfectly (lit. badly) clever, or educated.’ Râmarshi’s",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "other explanation is ज्ञानलवेनापि दरिद्रः which is not clear, and for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "which authority is required. Comp. “Little learning is a dangerous",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "thing.” It may be mentioned that the Stanza as spoken in conver-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "sation contains the तम् which our text has omitted.—Âryâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
